CRITICAL TECHNICAL ACCURACY

The current Slide 6 prototype:

- Uses synthetic claims and synthetic training data.
- Includes a genuinely working logistic regression classifier.
- Uses a binary Pend/Not Pend classification target.
- Does not establish validated prospective prediction on real production claims.
- Contains illustrative LLM-style explanations, not live LLM inference.

The proposed production architecture:

- Will use appropriately authorized historical claims and COB information.
- Will reconstruct features available before the adjudication attempt being predicted.
- Will compare rules, logistic regression, random forests, gradient boosting, and other justified models.
- Will apply appropriate cross-validation, temporal holdout testing, leakage controls, and cohort-specific evaluation.
- Will assess actionable risk identification at equivalent human-review capacity.
- Will use model-supported contributing factors and approved guidance to ground GenAI explanations.
- Will separately evaluate GenAI for factual accuracy, unsupported statements, consistency, reviewer usefulness, and operational benefit.
- Will retain human authorization for interventions and existing claims systems for adjudication.

Do not present proposed capabilities as already deployed or validated.

